KZ3 patch 2172 (RSX pass 159, renderer step 1 round R1): LD_FRONT_PROBE=1, measurement only (default off: one flag load per
hook). New GPU-free unit rsx_front_probe.h counts what a front/recorder split would have to snapshot and wait for: TEX bytes
and spans under the write-generation rule (counter-only, no copies), vertex/index bytes, FP misses (hash model of the front's
memcmp), main-memory ZPASS reports (class, has_val, OQ_NEVER, last-value hits, and the state-lag model against a mirror
published at the previous hard point), SYNC_BGS split by the front's drawn_since_wb bit, SYNC_WB, FLIP, draws before an
async ref publication, and a T = sum max(front+snap, rec) + drain model with the four step-1 gate booleans. One flip per
LD_FRONT_PROBE_N (default 100) is sampled: guest bytes are copied into a scratch buffer and the indices scanned, both timed,
and its words are replayed through a second dispatcher instance, timed. Prints [front-probe] lines on stderr. Hooks: ld_td_mark,
sink_end, after get_pso, rsx_live_draw_report_value, rsx_live_draw_before_guest_sync, rsx_live_draw_present,
rsx_live_draw_method (LD); nv0039_copy, gcm_ref_publish_one, the sync-hist event sites (CG, RC). Host test
tools/smoke/test_front_probe.sh.

